    pearls: "In DKA, insulin should NEVER be stopped if K+ is low (<3.3) — correct K+ first, then start insulin. Hypokalaemia with insulin therapy can cause fatal arrhythmias. Cerebral oedema is the most feared complication of DKA in children — monitor for headache, bradycardia, hypertension, GCS decline. Insulin drip should continue until anion gap closes, not just normoglycaemia.",
