    followUp: "Endocrine clinic in 4-6 weeks. Ophthalmology review for formal assessment and management of eye disease. Pregnancy counselling — must be euthyroid before conceiving (Carbimazole/PTU require adjustments).",
    pearls: "Graves disease is the most common cause of hyperthyroidism in iodine-sufficient areas. Propranolol provides rapid symptom relief but does not reduce hormone levels — it blocks adrenergic symptoms. Carbimazole/Methimazole are first-line thionamides (PTU is second-line due to hepatotoxicity risk). Agranulocytosis (risk 0.3-0.5%) presents with sudden fever/sore throat — warn every patient. RAI is contraindicated if active ophthalmopathy (can worsen it) or pregnancy.",
    references: ["ATA Guidelines: Hyperthyroidism", "ETA Guidelines: Graves Orbitopathy", "Kenya Clinical Guidelines: Thyroid Disease"],
